  "goodToKnow": "Das Blei is lead, the metal: schwer wie Blei (heavy as lead), bleifreies Benzin (unleaded petrol). Der Bleistift is a pencil, though pencils contain graphite, not lead. On New Year's Eve, Germans traditionally practised Bleigießen, melting lead shapes and dropping them in water to tell the future; since 2018, EU rules have banned lead sets, and wax or tin versions have replaced them. It has no plural."
